{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Reid&limit=10&title=Architects of the Web","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Architects of the Web ","subTitle":"1,000 days that built the future of business "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Reid, Robert,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1965-"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"1997"},"c1997"],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Wiley"}},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xliv, 370 p. : ill. ; 25 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"map"}}],"abstract":[{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Architects of the Web presents the history of the Web's creation and evolution - as well as its emergence as a dynamic business tool - through revealing profiles of its architects, the brilliant minds who have helped thrust the Web onto desktops and corporate agendas around the world. On the cutting edge of the online revolution, these visionaries have all made vital contributions to the advancement and enhancement of the Web that will define the way we conduct business."},{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In the future."}],"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Marc Andreesen : Netscape, portal to the web -- Rob Glaser : Progressive Networks, uniting sound with sites -- Kim Pole